{"files": [{"id": 39742909, "name": "LBNL_FDD_Dataset_SDAHU_all_3.zip", "size": 608146162, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/39742909", "supplied_md5": "f53a622b595c578a846a0d1988f8dc07", "computed_md5": "f53a622b595c578a846a0d1988f8dc07", "mimetype": "application/zip"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 14837629, "full_name": "Yimin Chen", "first_name": "Yimin", "last_name": "Chen", "is_active": true, "url_name": "Yimin_Chen", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 8368617, "full_name": "Jessica Granderson", "first_name": "Jessica", "last_name": "Granderson", "is_active": true, "url_name": "Jessica_Granderson", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://figshare.com/articles/dataset/LBNL_FDD_Dataset_SDAHU/22338283", "download_disabled": false, "description": "<p>The DOE and Berkeley Lab have partnered across the national laboratory complex and with the research community to curate, validate, and publish the world\u2019s largest set of labeled time-series data representing commercial HVAC systems operating in faulted and fault-free states.</p>\n<p>The data sets currently cover rooftop units, single-duct air handler units, dual-duct air handler units, variable air volume boxes, fan coil units, chiller plant, and boiler plant. Each data set includes from 20 to more than 100 data points that are commonly monitored in today\u2019s buildings. This operational data is paired with ground truth information indicating which faults are present during which time periods.</p>", "funding": "U.S. Department of Energy under Contract No. DE-AC02-05CH11231", "funding_list": [{"id": 20885922, "title": "U.S. Department of Energy under Contract No. DE-AC02-05CH11231", "grant_code": "", "funder_name": null, "is_user_defined": 1}], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 608146162, "created_date": "2023-03-27T19:39:52Z", "modified_date": "2023-03-27T19:39:52Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record"